WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
Speaker 1: This is super interesting. Many of you&nbsp;
know about Republican Congressman Kevin McCarthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:11.440
now Kevin McCarthy is a guy who back around the&nbsp;
Trump riots, was speaking regularly not only with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.680
Donald Trump but with other people in that circle.&nbsp;
And CNN has unearthed audio of Kevin McCarthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:24.160
saying I spoke to Trump, and Trump admitted he&nbsp;
has some responsibility for the riots to me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:30.320
Now, why is this relevant? It's relevant because&nbsp;
for the last year plus now, year in two weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.720
almost to the day Donald Trump and people around&nbsp;
him have been denying that Trump had anything to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:44.160
do with what ultimately took place and or saying&nbsp;
it was peaceful and or saying the violence was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.240
antifa. So all of those different things conflict.&nbsp;
Some of them cancel each other out doesn't matter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.200
The point is, they've gone out of their way to&nbsp;
say, Trump. There's no responsibility here for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.600
Trump whatsoever, for what happened on January&nbsp;
6th and yet. And yet, CNN unearths audio of Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:08.880
McCarthy saying Trump admitted responsibility&nbsp;
for the riot. CNN's K File resurfaced the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:15.680
House Republicans comments to a California radio&nbsp;
station days after the Jan. six insurrection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.040
Let's just listen to the audio. Take a&nbsp;
listen to exactly what Kevin McCarthy said.&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.280
Speaker 3: I say he has a responsibility.&nbsp;
He told me personally that he does have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.840
responsibility. I think a lot of people do what I&nbsp;
proposed, which I think history will say I'm right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:37.040
because it's the right thing to do. I believe have&nbsp;
a bipartisan commission and get all your facts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.240
actually work through the grand jury to&nbsp;
find out at the end instead of determining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.000
whether someone's guilty or not.
Speaker 1: Pretty. Wow. I mean, it's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.120
only a good idea to have a special committee do&nbsp;
a special investigation while it's happening now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.320
and Republicans are essentially completely&nbsp;
opposed to it. But Kevin McCarthy clearly says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:03.920
I believe Trump has some responsibility. And Trump&nbsp;
admitted to me that he has some responsibility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:10.000
This has been completely buried now. Kevin&nbsp;
McCarthy was more recently asked about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.120
He forgot guys he doesn't remember. Kevin&nbsp;
McCarthy says he doesn't remember the phone call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:21.360
where Trump admitted some responsibility days&nbsp;
after January 6th. House Minority Leader Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:26.240
McCarthy told other Republicans in a phone&nbsp;
call that Trump claimed some responsibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:31.120
for the Capitol riot, according to CNN. But&nbsp;
during a news conference Thursday, McCarthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.840
said he couldn't recall the phone call. Here is&nbsp;
Kevin McCarthy asked about it. Check this out!&nbsp;

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.920
Speaker 2: Did you tell House Republicans&nbsp;
on a January 11 phone call that President&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:44.320
Trump told you? He agreed that he bore&nbsp;
some responsibility for January 6th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:49.840
as Chairman Thompson's letter indicates.&nbsp;
I'm not sure what call you're talking about.&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.120
Speaker 1: And then he goes on to a different&nbsp;
reporter. Now, notice the very specific language.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:03.680
I don't know what call you are talking about.&nbsp;
That's a very different answer than I have never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:11.520
said nor believed. Trump admitted responsibility,&nbsp;
nor is responsible. So if someone said to me. Did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.840
you say that and I go, I don't know what phone&nbsp;
call you're talking about. It's not a denial.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:22.880
Right. Sort of like if someone says, Hey,&nbsp;
did you um, did did you call and threaten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:30.160
to steal pizza from a Pizza Hut? And I go, I&nbsp;
don't know what phone call you're referring to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.000
That's a very different answer. Then I've never&nbsp;
called Pizza Hut and threaten to steal pizza.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.280
These are two very, very different reactions.&nbsp;
And Kevin McCarthy. Listen, if you have to guess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:46.000
what the truth is, the truth is, at the time, it&nbsp;
wasn't yet clear that for a year, Trump and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.840
people around him would deny that he had anything&nbsp;
to do with the riot. So Kevin McCarthy said it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:58.640
early January, mid-January of 2021 and meant&nbsp;
it, and it was true. And now, in retrospect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.760
it would look very, very bad for McCarthy&nbsp;
to say this last year of Trump and everybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.200
around him pretending like he had nothing to&nbsp;
do with it. And there's nothing to see here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.280
Well, a year ago, Trump admitted to me that he&nbsp;
had some responsibility that would look very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.840
very bad for Trump, and it would probably put&nbsp;
Kevin McCarthy in the doghouse. So I believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:22.160
that Trump did say it. I believe McCarthy did&nbsp;
report it at the time, and now he's just lying.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.680
And it's such a technical and specific&nbsp;
answer. I don't know what phone call you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:35.840
are referring to is a world away from. I've never&nbsp;
said it because Trump never said it to me, and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.920
don't believe that he bears any responsibility.&nbsp;
Those are dramatically different things

